            <div xml:id="d70">

                <pb facs="0143" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 70.</note>
                <head>Mr. E. B. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 274.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-09-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 2, 1870</date>. (Received September
                    15.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to inclose you herewith copies of telegraphic dispatches from
                    Count Bismarck to Count Bernstorff, sent to me by Mr. Motley, to be by me
                    transmitted to the French government, together with my notes accompanying the
                    same.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>







